claim.claim-text:
an input port (126a) provided to one side of the swelling absorption pad (126) in the longitudinal direction;
an output port (126b) provided to the other side of the swelling absorption pad (126) in the longitudinal direction; and
a cooling portion (126c) configured to connect the input port (126a) and the output port (126b) to each other and having a greater sectional area than the input port (126a) and the output port (126b).

a rack housing (110);
a plurality of air-cooled battery packs (120) stacked in the rack housing (110);
a water tank (130) configured to store a water coolant and disposed above a module stack including the plurality of battery packs (120) and configured to store a coolant;
a coolant tube (150) configured to connect the water tank (130) and the battery pack (120) to each other;
at least one sensor (160) installed inside the rack housing (110) to detect a thermal runaway phenomenon occurring in at least a part of the plurality of battery packs (120); and
a controller (140) configured to output a control signal for introducing a water coolant into the battery pack (120) through the coolant tube (150) when a thermal runaway phenomenon is detected by the sensor (160),
each battery pack (120) comprising:

an air inlet (124) formed through the pack housing (123) at one side of the unit module stack in a stacking direction;
an air outlet (125) formed through the pack housing (123) at the other side of the unit module stack in the stacking direction; and
an expansion pad (127) disposed inside the air inlet (124) and the air outlet (125) and configured to expand due to the contact with moisture of a water coolant introduced into the battery pack (120) to close the air inlet (124) and the air outlet (125).

an input port (126a) provided to one side of the swelling absorption pad (126) in the longitudinal direction;
an output port (126b) provided to the other side of the swelling absorption pad (126) in the longitudinal direction; and
a cooling portion (126c) configured to connect the input port (126a) and the output port (126b) to each other and having a greater sectional area than the input port (126a) and the output port (126b).
